(7610102, 1230694, 112739, '<td valign="top">Very well done! And since you planned the creation of the image, it is that much more gratifying. Big congrats for the well deserved win!</td>', 'Very well done! And since you planned the creation of the image, it is that much more gratifying. Big congrats for the well deserved win!', '2019-01-23 13:02:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(7610103, 1231039, 112739, '<td valign="top">Very Mary Ann image! I knew it would do well. I love exploring and experiencing your creations.  Congrats on the yellow!</td>', 'Very Mary Ann image! I knew it would do well. I love exploring and experiencing your creations.  Congrats on the yellow!', '2019-01-23 13:05:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(7610105, 1231090, 112739, '<td valign="top">Congrats on HM Alessandro!</td>', 'Congrats on HM Alessandro!', '2019-01-23 13:06:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(7610106, 1230777, 112739, '<td valign="top">Very creative. Love the implied and unexpected animation.</td>', 'Very creative. Love the implied and unexpected animation.', '2019-01-23 13:08:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(7610109, 1230777, 115814, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by posthumous:</b></div><hr/><i> very creative, taking one symbol and turning it into the opposite symbol.<br/> <br/>well dang, this was one of my favorites and now I see it''s a copy of something on shutterstock. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Sorry... I can''t claim the idea as an original. I don''t use or visit Shutterstock, and frankly, don''t remember where/when I originally saw something <i>like</i> this. I created it with the intent of honing some compositing skills and representing a concept about freedom that I thought was particularly germane in our current environment. <br/> <br/>So... <br/> <br/>Derivative? Yep. No objection to that characterization. <br/>Shameless copy? Not a chance.<br/>Demonstration of improved PP abilities? Absolutely.<br/>Happy with the result/score: Affirmative<br/>Art? Hmmm... I guess that''s a question for the beholder.<br/> <br/>Thanks for the comments. It''s alright with me if it''s still one of your favorites :-) <br/> <br/>Or not.<br/> <br/>[Edited for minor typos]<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2019-01-23 13:39:31.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by posthumous: very creative, taking one symbol and turning it into the opposite symbol. well dang, this was one of my favorites and now I see it''s a copy of something on shutterstock.   Sorry... I can''t claim the idea as an original. I don''t use or visit Shutterstock, and frankly, don''t remember where/when I originally saw something like this. I created it with the intent of honing some compositing skills and representing a concept about freedom that I thought was particularly germane in our current environment.  So...  Derivative? Yep. No objection to that characterization. Shameless copy? Not a chance.Demonstration of improved PP abilities? Absolutely.Happy with the result/score: AffirmativeArt? Hmmm... I guess that''s a question for the beholder. Thanks for the comments. It''s alright with me if it''s still one of your favorites :-)  Or not. [Edited for minor typos]', '2019-01-23 13:38:39.000000', '2019-01-23 13:39:31.000000', 0),
(7610124, 1230521, 86447, '<td valign="top">"It was the 2 voter, that robbed me my first blue in an art challenge. I hope they did it because they hated it and not because they had a horse in the race."<br/> <br/>I never vote an image down to raise my score.   Seems criminal.   Don''t vote if you can''t vote fairly.<br/> <br/>Congratulations on your "near BLUE"!   :D<br/> <br/>This is beautiful.<br/> <br/></td>', '"It was the 2 voter, that robbed me my first blue in an art challenge. I hope they did it because they hated it and not because they had a horse in the race." I never vote an image down to raise my score.   Seems criminal.   Don''t vote if you can''t vote fairly. Congratulations on your "near BLUE"!   :D This is beautiful. ', '2019-01-23 15:51:46.000000', NULL, 0),
